/**
 * Test moderator's ability to update the rationale for a comment edit (revision history) entry.
 *
 * Business Context:
 * Moderators sometimes need to edit the rationale for a comment edit (e.g., for audit correction, compliance, or moderators' intervention in content discussions).
 * Only the rationale (edit_reason) can be updated; all other edit record fields are immutable via this API.
 * The system must audit who made the update and when, and enforce that only allowed fields are changed.
 *
 * Steps:
 * 1. Register a new moderator, then log in as this moderator.
 * 2. Register a normal member, then log in as this member.
 * 3. Member creates a new post in a random category.
 * 4. Member creates a new comment under the post.
 * 5. Member edits their comment (generating an initial comment edit record; this gives us a comment with at least one edit revision).
 * 6. Moderator logs in again (switch context) to perform the audit update.
 * 7. Moderator updates the rationale (edit_reason) of the initial comment edit record.
 * 8. Verify only the rationale changes, all other fields (edit_body, etc.) remain the same.
 * 9. Check audit information: date, editor_member_id matches moderator (if supported).
 *10. Attempt to update a non-existent comment edit ID and assert rejection.
 *
 * Note: API/DTO does not allow updating immutable fields like edit_body. Also, edit record listing/fetching is not available; we use the commentId as a stand-in for editId for test purposes.
 */
