 *   5. Moderator can upvote (+1) on a post, and duplicate upvotes are rejected
 *   6. Moderator cannot downvote the same post after upvoting (one vote per post per moderator)
 *   7. Moderator can downvote (-1) a different post, and duplicate downvotes/upvotes on same post are rejected
 *   8. All major responses are type-asserted and business rules, including error cases, are enforced
 *
 * Steps:
 *   1. Register and login a new moderator with random email and display name
 *   2. Register and login a member
 *   3. Member creates first post (for upvote)
 *   4. Switch to moderator, upvote the post, verify response
 *   5. Attempt duplicate upvote and then a downvote on the same post — both must fail
 *   6. Member creates a second post
