 *
 * 1. Admin registration and login, establishing a valid admin session for the test.
 * 2. Attempting to fetch a report with random UUIDs for both postId and reportId (which are extremely unlikely to correspond to actual records), and confirming an error is thrown (i.e., not found or similar).
 * 3. Simulating an unauthenticated (non-admin) request by removing the Authorization token from the connection headers, and verifying the endpoint correctly blocks access (error is thrown).
 *
 * Notes:
 * - It is not feasible to trigger a malformed-UUID runtime error because the TypeScript signature enforces UUID format at compile-time (i.e., format errors are prevented statically, not caught at runtime).
 * - Error validation uses TestValidator.error, only confirming that an error is thrown, not inspecting the error details in depth.
