 *
 * This test asserts end-to-end the access control and information fidelity of the endpoint for admin audit and moderation.
 *
 * Steps:
 * 1. Register a new admin user (and get admin email/password). 
 * 2. Login as admin (ensure privileged tokens are set for the connection).
 * 3. Register a new member user for post/comment creation (keep member's credentials for login).
 * 4. Login as member to establish context for board posting.
 * 5. Create a new post as the member (get postId).
 * 6. Write a comment to the post as the member (get commentId).
 * 7. Edit the comment as the member (use put to create an edit history entry, get commentEditId from the response or later retrieval).
 * 8. Switch back to the admin session (login as admin again if needed).
 * 9. Use the admin endpoint GET /polEcoBoard/admin/posts/{postId}/comments/{commentId}/commentEdits/{commentEditId} to retrieve the edit audit record.
 * 10. Assert the returned field fidelity: edit_body matches edit, editor_member_id is member, correct timestamps, and edit_reason (if set) is present.
 *
 * This covers both positive path (proper admin access and detail fields present) and validates intended access-control logic in the system.
